        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4a6b785d-4fc2-5ca2-8575-74a8178a4a60",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vincent Sherman, David Seltzer, William Dozier\n- Films: Mr. Skeffington, Nora Prentiss, The Young Philadelphians, The Omen, Bird on a Wire, Lucas, Punchline, Shining Through, Harriet Craig\n- Companies: Columbia Pictures\n\nFacts:\n- Vincent Sherman directed the films \"Mr. Skeffington\" in 1944, \"Nora Prentiss\" in 1947, and \"The Young Philadelphians\" in 1959.\n- David Seltzer, born in 1940, is an American screenwriter, producer, and director.\n- David Seltzer is best known for writing the screenplays for \"The Omen\" in 1976 and \"Bird on a Wire\" in 1990.\n- As writer-director, David Seltzer made the 1986 teen tragi-comedy \"Lucas,\" the 1988 comedy \"Punchline,\" and the 1992 film \"Shining Through.\"\n- The film \"Harriet Craig\" was directed by Vincent Sherman, produced by William Dozier, and distributed by Columbia Pictures.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
